title: Global shell › Top bar › Ask FLO › Answers that read the screen
route: Every page (Ask FLO drawer)
intro: Five of FLO's rules read the demo data for one case, one payer or one screen: what is missing, when an authorization ends, what a payer requires, which reviews are due, which patients need a fix before billing. When the question names a case ('R-1042') FLO uses it; otherwise it uses the case page that is open; otherwise the request that needs you first. Each answer names the case, quotes live data and ends with a link to the exact place. They are recommendations, never payer facts.
dir: TD
also: The short line 'This is FLO's reading of the demo data, not a payer confirmation.' appears once, under the answers that read payer rules, coverage or an authorization. The numbers and the wording are computed when the question is asked.
---
start s1 "A question reaches one of the five rules\n(a chip for the screen, or typed text)"
decision d0 "Which key words?"

group gM "Missing: 'What is missing for R-1042?'"
  decision m1 "Which case?\nNamed in the question, else the open case page, else the request that needs you first"
  agent m2 "FLO reads the case's draft\nOpen items still unresolved, by kind: Missing, To settle, Risk\nThe payer's document count from the saved Payers list"
  decision m3 "Was the request already sent?"
  toast m4 "'Nothing is missing for R-0870 (Summit, Residential 3.5). It was already sent, so it is with Summit and Navigator is tracking it.'"
  toast m5 "'R-1042 (Summit, Residential 3.5) has 3 open items in the draft.'\n'To settle: One date conflict needs your answer ...'\n'Risk: Relapse risk is high without a named step-down.'\n'Missing: A therapy note from the last 14 days is missing (8 of 9 Summit documents).'\n'Summit asks for 9 documents at Residential 3.5.'\nFLO's reading line"
  click ml "Click 'Open R-1042, Recommended actions'"
endgroup

group gX "Expiry: 'When does this authorization run out?'"
  agent x1 "FLO reads the Case Manager ledger row of the case and its next unsigned review"
  decision x2 "What does the row hold?"
  toast x3 "End date: 'I-2207 (Cardinal, IOP) has used 38 of 48 units. The authorization ends in 3 days (Fri 10/23).'\n'Its next clinical review is Wed 10/21, 4:00 pm.'"
  toast x4 "Measured in units, no date: 'has used 16 of 48 units, so 32 units are left. The ledger holds no end date for it.'"
  toast x5 "Other next event: 'has used 14 of 14 days. The approved days are used up. The payer's decision on the next stay is expected Thu 10/22.'\nNo approval yet: 'has no approval yet, so there is nothing to run out.'"
  click xl "Click 'Open I-2207'"
endgroup

group gR "Requires: 'What does Summit require?'"
  agent r1 "FLO reads the payer's saved configuration on Payers\nThe payer is named in the question, else the open case's payer"
  toast r2 "On a case page: 'I-2207: Cardinal Health Plan asks for 6 documents at IOP: ASAM multidimensional assessment, ... and 2 more.'\nOtherwise: 'asks for 9 documents at Residential 3.5, 6 at IOP, 7 at PHP and 8 at Detox.'\n'Timing: ...' and 'After a denial: ...'\n'A change waits for you: Criteria changed, version 2026.3' when one is unacknowledged"
  click rl "Click 'Open Payers, Cardinal, Documents'"
endgroup

group gV "Reviews: 'Which reviews are due?'"
  agent v1 "FLO reads this week's clinical reviews that are not signed"
  toast v2 "'47 reviews are due this week, 5 of them due now or overdue: 35 drafted (29 clean), 4 not drafted yet, 8 need a clinician's update.'\n'Next: ...' and 'Needs your update: R-0912, R-0899, R-0881, and 5 more.'"
  click vl "Click 'Open R-0912, review'"
endgroup

group gE "Eligibility: 'Which patients need a fix before billing?'"
  agent e1 "FLO reads the coverage checks and their verdicts"
  toast e2 "'5 patients need a fix before billing.'\nOne line each, in the screen's order: 'R-0921 (J.D., Cardinal): 14 of 14 days used.' 'R-1118 (A.F., Beacon): the plan does not cover the service.' 'I-2275 (E.K., Summit): another plan pays first.'\nFLO's reading line"
  click el "Click 'Open R-0921 in Eligibility & Benefits'"
endgroup

endx n1 "Nothing to read: 'I did not find R-9999 in the demo data.' or 'Tell me which payer, for example: What does Summit require?'\nThe chips for the screen stay under it"

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Recommended actions › The tab"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › Documents › Read the document list"
goto g4 "Continues in: Case Manager › Reviews this week › The review drawer"
goto g5 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › What the page shows"

s1 --> d0
d0 -->|missing, incomplete| m1
d0 -->|expir, run out, units, end| x1
d0 -->|require| r1
d0 -->|review| v1
d0 -->|billing, eligib, fix before| e1
m1 -->|Found| m2 --> m3
m1 -->|No such case| n1
m3 -->|Yes| m4 --> ml
m3 -->|No| m5 --> ml
ml --> g1
x1 --> x2
x2 -->|Expiry date| x3 --> xl
x2 -->|Units only| x4 --> xl
x2 -->|Anything else| x5 --> xl
xl --> g2
r1 --> r2 --> rl --> g3
r1 -.-> n1
v1 --> v2 --> vl --> g4
e1 --> e2 --> el --> g5
